>> title: Fish Taco Bowl
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: cod, rice, cabbage, blackened, mexican, skillet, bowl
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: fish taco bowl, baja bowl, blackened fish bowl, fish bowl, taco bowl, rice bowl, fish tacos without the tortilla
>> pairs-with: cajun-seasoning, crema-mexicana, salsa-verde-cruda, guacamole
>> servings: 4
>> time: 50 min
>> slack: narrow — cod is done as the flakes part, and a minute past that it dries out and shreds into the rice
>> step.1: Blackening is a spice crust, not burnt fish. The pan has to be hot enough to toast the rub before the fillet cooks through, which is about three minutes a side and the extractor fan on high.
>> step.2: simmer 18 min, rest 10 min, lime last
>> step.3: press the rub on
>> step.4: sear 6 min in a smoking pan
>> step.5: macerate 15 min, until it slumps
>> step.6: build it, fish along one side

Blackening is a spice crust, not burnt fish. The pan has to be hot enough to toast the rub before the fillet cooks through, which is about three minutes a side and the extractor fan on high.

Simmer @long-grain white rice{1 1/4%cups}(250 g; rinsed) in @water{2%cups}(475 mL) with @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} covered ~simmer{18%min}, then ~rest{10%min} off the heat and fork through @lime{1}(juiced).

Coat @cod fillets{1 1/2%lb}(680 g; in 4 pieces) in @cajun seasoning{2%Tbs} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, pressing it onto both faces.

Sear @&(~1)cod{} in a smoking-hot #cast iron skillet{} ~sear{6%min}, turning once, until the crust is near black and the fish flakes at the thick end, then break it into large pieces.

Toss @red cabbage{3%cups}(shredded fine) with @lime{1}(juiced), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @cilantro{1/3%cup}(chopped), then leave it to ~macerate{15%min}, until it slumps and turns bright.

Spoon @&(~4)lime rice{} into four bowls, pile @&(~1)cabbage{} along one side and @&(~2)blackened cod{} along the other, and finish with @avocado{1}(sliced), @pickled jalapeños{2%Tbs} and @lime{1}(in wedges).
